WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.849
Across the board,

00:00:03.929 --> 00:00:07.778
Moccasin solves the rematerialization problem
substantially faster than Checkmate,

00:00:07.858 --> 00:00:11.707
up to an order of magnitude on the larger graphs.

00:00:11.787 --> 00:00:15.636
On the smallest graph the two are comparable, but
the gap widens quickly.

00:00:15.716 --> 00:00:19.565
For the graph with two hundred fifty nodes and a
tight memory budget,

00:00:19.645 --> 00:00:23.495
Checkmate fails to find any feasible solution
within thirty minutes,

00:00:23.575 --> 00:00:27.424
and at the loosest budget it takes ten minutes,
while Moccasin finishes in seconds.

00:00:27.504 --> 00:00:31.353
For the five hundred and one thousand node graphs,
Checkmate times out entirely,

00:00:31.433 --> 00:00:35.282
finding no solution even given three hours, and it
exits with an out-of-memory error,

00:00:35.362 --> 00:00:39.211
whereas Moccasin converges to a good,

00:00:39.291 --> 00:00:43.140
low-duration-increase solution in under an hour.
